## Quick Reference: Secure vs Insecure

### ❌ INSECURE - Data Leakage

```typescript
// WRONG - Fetches ALL tasks from ALL foundries
const { data: tasks } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .select('*')

// WRONG - Fetches ALL profiles from ALL companies
const { data: members } = await supabase
    .from('profiles')
    .select('id, full_name, role')

// WRONG - Fetches ALL objectives from ALL foundries
const { data: objectives } = await supabase
    .from('objectives')
    .select('*')
```

### ✅ SECURE - Proper Isolation

```typescript
// Get user's foundry_id first
const { data: userProfile } = await supabase
    .from('profiles')
    .select('foundry_id')
    .eq('id', user.id)
    .single()

const foundry_id = userProfile?.foundry_id
if (!foundry_id) return <Error />

// Filter ALL queries by foundry_id
const { data: tasks } = await supabase
    .from('tasks')
    .select('*')
    .eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)  // ✅ CRITICAL

const { data: members } = await supabase
    .from('profiles')
    .select('id, full_name, role')
    .eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)  // ✅ CRITICAL

const { data: objectives } = await supabase
    .from('objectives')
    .select('*')
    .eq('foundry_id', foundry_id)  // ✅ CRITICAL
```

